{"kind":"request","text":"Replace the duplicate Mine and single Topic-author controls with one roster-complete People multi-select whose explicit scope distinguishes current responsibility, topic authorship, and involvement.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-work-people-filters","conditions":"The standalone Mine button and single-select Topic author control are removed; one compact People control opens a keyboard-operable multi-select menu populated from the complete durable actor roster supplied by #2787 rather than only current topic authors or locally custodial actors; the menu explicitly chooses one filter scope at a time: Current responsibility, Topic author, or Any involvement, and never presents an unlabeled actor checklist whose meaning must be guessed; Current responsibility is the default and uses the same lifecycle mapping as Needs my action—open work belongs to the addressed actor, promised work to the performer, and reported work to the requester awaiting review—while terminal work has no current responsible actor; Topic author means only the actor who wrote the root request/proposal that defines the topic; Any involvement matches a work item when a selected actor is its topic author, requester, addressed actor, performer, report author, or other structurally recorded participant, with those facets computed from the projection rather than text mentions; actors selected within one scope combine with OR; the closed menu summarizes All people, one actor name, or an exact count and scope, provides Select all, Clear, and Only me conveniences inside the menu, and exposes active selections as removable state without restoring a duplicate Mine control; in Topics presentation, Topic author removes whole topics, while Current responsibility and Any involvement filter item rows/cards and retain the topic header as causal context whenever at least one item remains; topic counts clearly reflect the filtered subset and may show “N of M” when useful; Board applies the same item semantics; opening Thread or Railway from filtered work always shows the complete causal thread and is never pruned by a Work retrieval filter; Needs my action remains a distinct personal responsibility preset and composes predictably with People, lifecycle, search, unread, and following filters, with contradictory selections producing an honest empty state and individually clearable filter chips; Other attention is no longer silently discarded whenever a people filter is active as the current author filter does—rows use a documented applicable actor facet, and rows with no facet are represented by an explicit Unassigned/other choice rather than disappearing by accident; active actors are primary in the checklist, retired actors use #2786's hidden-history pattern, duplicate display names remain distinguishable by kind and short fingerprint, and no selection changes actor identity or durable state; focused projection tests pin the three scope definitions across open/promised/reported/closed work, nested topics, multiple actors, duplicate names, Other attention, and filter composition; component tests cover menu/checklist behavior, summaries, only-me/select-all/clear, list/board parity, complete threads, empty states, focus/escape/outside-click behavior, narrow layouts, and accessibility; the embedded UI is rebuilt; relevant UI and Go gates pass; an independent agent approves the exact implementation head before merge.","depends_on":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:70a76f6cca7f42cfc24f5fac62f09ffeadc15698","priority":"minor-usability","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}